# A program address used as a branch target prints bare; one read as data is
# wrapped; MAC qualifies it with the page instead. dis2000 draws the same
# three-way distinction, and collapsing it is what a single operand kind gets
# wrong. The address itself is scaled from words to bytes, as everywhere else in
# this engine, so 0x7700 in the encoding prints as 0xee00.
d "mac p, @0x00, 0:0xee00" 00140077 0x0
